From 1fc545b517e9cc04b3801b448bd1f1bf8bf445d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:52:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] newsletter: fix re-subscribe, send reliability, unsubscribe
 security

- subscribe: re-subscribing after unsubscribing no longer falls through to
  an insert that hits the unique email constraint; it reissues a token and
  sends the confirmation email
- confirm: links expire after 7 days (as the email says); an expired pending
  signup gets a fresh token
- unsubscribe: uses a secret per-subscriber unsubscribe_token instead of the
  plain email, so links can't be used to unsubscribe someone else
- send: use Resend batch API (100/call) with per-day idempotency keys,
  check Resend's returned error instead of treating every resolved call as
  sent, exit non-zero on failures, add List-Unsubscribe header
- send: escape AI/RSS text and drop non-http links in the email HTML
- send: never email mock data on a real send; skip weeks with no usable
  items; unmatched Google News items are OTHER, not CDSCO
- preview: PREVIEW_TO env var and [PREVIEW] subject prefix
- Groq model id updated to groq/compound-mini (as in news_pipeline)
- supabase-setup.sql: adds unsubscribe_token + token_issued_at columns

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EEK9AFe8Vc33tAFbe3z2u5
